                        "form": "галдежа́х"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37abeb7e-20c6-3652-8914-8dd67d1f6ca1",
                        "entry_id": "fc3970fe-f28b-3445-9866-3ba138c81be7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг.-сниж. действие по значению гл. галдеть; беспорядочные крики нескольких людей или животных"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ac6d81d-c67b-44ae-ac84-031294bf8c43",
                                "sense_id": "37abeb7e-20c6-3652-8914-8dd67d1f6ca1",
                                "text": "Когда впоследствии ямщики подняли обычные споры из-за очереди и разверстки, ― он слушал этот галдёж равнодушно и отчасти насмешливо."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6987ea42-6cce-4e58-8ed2-c1f6a4d8e9f2",
                                "sense_id": "37abeb7e-20c6-3652-8914-8dd67d1f6ca1",
                                "text": "За сценой крики, звон, страшный шум, галдёж, падение"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a98c8ce2-fa5b-408e-92ad-13d6c7559223",
                                "sense_id": "37abeb7e-20c6-3652-8914-8dd67d1f6ca1",
                                "text": "Цапли, дикие утки и какая-то птичка из породы бекасовых проснулись и завели свой музыкальный галдёж…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5da2a026-dfe8-40e6-94b5-e65749352723",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc3970fe-f28b-3445-9866-3ba138c81be7",
                        "source_sense_id": "37abeb7e-20c6-3652-8914-8dd67d1f6ca1",
                        "target_lang_word": "tumult",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tumult",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b97dd9b2-3c19-3bf2-8bf3-ba41808adc55",
                                        "entry_id": "2f815fab-bb5a-3419-9279-607fedac6d04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Confused, agitated noise as made by a crowd."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b7d4638-d9c2-4e7c-bd94-5d411ef44a44",
                                                "sense_id": "b97dd9b2-3c19-3bf2-8bf3-ba41808adc55",
                                                "text": "Till in loud tumult all the Greeks arose."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e679704a-5811-3038-a222-b9eea2893d45",
                                        "entry_id": "2f815fab-bb5a-3419-9279-607fedac6d04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Violent commotion or agitation, often with confusion of sounds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a44b4e3e-2009-4651-b5e1-773a13ade2ba",
                                                "sense_id": "e679704a-5811-3038-a222-b9eea2893d45",
                                                "text": "the tumult of the elements"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa8577ef-2c79-48b1-9efb-b6e56dc248ba",
                                                "sense_id": "e679704a-5811-3038-a222-b9eea2893d45",
                                                "text": "the tumult of the spirits or passions"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa23f013-63d8-4e68-beb2-7d0584af35e1",
                                                "sense_id": "e679704a-5811-3038-a222-b9eea2893d45",
                                                "text": "This is what I wanted my story 'Snapshot' to sound like — a very cold surface, with heat and passion beneath. The icy surface is going to break and you're totally engulfed in the tumult."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f619fe9b-01ef-4f7b-b730-ebd109a7a6b0",
                                                "sense_id": "e679704a-5811-3038-a222-b9eea2893d45",
                                                "text": "Football is a game of tumult and glory, of small disappointments and lingering dreams, and Mata has played long enough at the highest level to appreciate these truths."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1293b94-cae9-380c-af57-d7d635b857ab",
                                        "entry_id": "2f815fab-bb5a-3419-9279-607fedac6d04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A riot or uprising."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tumult",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19506ea4-6506-3167-92d8-9e414282101c",
                                        "entry_id": "596e26fd-3cff-347b-a783-eb98b8af24a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a tumult; to be in great commotion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a27a64c7-d3da-4c46-9f79-a2b6dc7ed387",
                                                "sense_id": "19506ea4-6506-3167-92d8-9e414282101c",
                                                "text": "Importuning and tumulting even to the fear of a revolt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6d056f5d-d64b-4266-bf86-5e206c48b0b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc3970fe-f28b-3445-9866-3ba138c81be7",
                        "source_sense_id": "37abeb7e-20c6-3652-8914-8dd67d1f6ca1",
                        "target_lang_word": "pandemonium",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pandemonium",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6942b88b-cf6d-3c99-8edb-9d3d07932323",
                                        "entry_id": "03a57d43-3ef8-36a7-a6f7-633d5a7818ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A loud, wild, tumultuous protest, disorder, or chaotic situation, usually of a crowd, often violent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2aba42f4-f0ee-4833-bcda-1e0bfc319395",
                                                "sense_id": "6942b88b-cf6d-3c99-8edb-9d3d07932323",
                                                "text": "Whatever all this pandemonium means, I suppose the police station will help us."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7af9ec8e-fe7c-40c5-a6b1-9f8539e6681e",
                                                "sense_id": "6942b88b-cf6d-3c99-8edb-9d3d07932323",
                                                "text": "Whenever you have violent pandemonium, there's the overwhelming possibility for panic and tragedy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1621edf-11f4-34c3-a606-15b92149e979",
                                        "entry_id": "03a57d43-3ef8-36a7-a6f7-633d5a7818ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An outburst; loud, riotous uproar, especially of a crowd."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a540253a-891d-434d-ab07-744a57e8fe64",
                                                "sense_id": "d1621edf-11f4-34c3-a606-15b92149e979",
                                                "text": "Riyad Mahrez flighted the free-kick that followed to the far post and Morgan, with not much finesse but plenty of desire, bundled the ball over the line. Cue pandemonium in the stands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
